---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="The Antichrist and the Prophet — Dale Joseph"
  description="A political and spiritual thriller about power, prophecy, and the battle for the soul of the world. Coming 2026 from Dale Joseph."
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="section book-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label gold">A Novel</p>
      <h1>The Antichrist<br />and the Prophet</h1>
      <p class="byline">by Dale Joseph</p>
      <span class="status-badge">Available Now · Kindle</span>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="logline">
        The line between prophet and Antichrist<br />has never been thinner.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H4BQPW8V" class="btn btn--filled" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buy on Amazon →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PREMISE -->
  <section class="section premise">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="premise-body">
        <p>
          The world is fracturing. Democracies are falling. A President who
          has long since stopped distinguishing between his ambitions and his
          convictions is consolidating power at home and abroad — and growing
          into something the old language barely has words for.
        </p>
        <p>
          From a cramped apartment, during the silence of a global pandemic,
          a different voice begins to rise. He is a failed actor and an
          abandoned student of law and politics. He writes at two in the
          morning because he has nowhere else to put what he carries. Millions
          of people read him. Then millions more.
        </p>
        <p>
          He calls himself One. A man called the Baptist tells him he is
          chosen — the one who will unite humanity, prepare the way. One does
          not feel chosen. He feels like a man who has failed at almost
          everything and stumbled onto the one thing he cannot abandon.
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          "I never asked for this. I am not a saint. I am not even a believer
          in the way you are. Why me?"
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          What follows is the story of two men in a country that could still
          go either way — and the ancient question neither of them can answer:
          the man who comes to prepare the way, is he the prophet? Or the most
          dangerous kind of true believer?
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TWO FIGURES -->
  <section class="section section--dark figures-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <div class="figures">
        <div class="figure">
          <p class="figure-label gold">One</p>
          <p>
            He began as a footnote. A failed actor. A man writing philosophy
            into the void at two in the morning because there was nowhere else
            to put his grief. Then the world started reading him. Then the
            world started following him. He believes he was sent. He fears he
            is becoming what he was sent to stop.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="figure">
          <p class="figure-label gold">The President</p>
          <p>
            He does not think of himself as a destroyer. He thinks of himself
            as a necessary man. He speaks of order, borders, and reclaimed
            greatness. His followers hear courage. His opponents see cruelty.
            Both are missing something. What he is, precisely, is a man who
            stopped distinguishing between his ambitions and his convictions —
            and has not noticed the difference since.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT THE BOOK IS -->
  <section class="section about-book">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>What This Book Is</h2>
      <p>
        A political thriller and a spiritual reckoning. A story about power
        and prophecy — about what happens when a movement built on hope begins
        to resemble the thing it is fighting. About a mentor stolen and
        returned. About a woman who loved the right man and the wrong father,
        and understood the difference before either of them did.
      </p>
      <p>
        And about the question at the center of it all: in the last days, how
        do you tell the prophet from the Antichrist — when one of them is
        asking the same question about himself?
      </p>
      <div class="themes">
        <div class="theme">
          <h3 class="gold">Power</h3>
          <p>What it does to the men who seek it — and the men who never wanted it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="theme">
          <h3 class="gold">Prophecy</h3>
          <p>Whether a calling and a wound are the same thing, in the right century.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="theme">
          <h3 class="gold">Rebirth</h3>
          <p>Some endings look like ruin before they reveal themselves as beginnings.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EMAIL SIGNUP -->
  <section class="section section--dark email-capture" id="notify">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>Be First to Know</h2>
      <p>
        When <em>The Antichrist and the Prophet</em> is ready, you will hear
        it here first — along with excerpts and the story of how it was written.
        No noise. Just the work.
      </p>
      <form
        action="https://formspree.io/f/maqpvlgz"
        method="POST"
        class="email-form"
      >
        <input type="hidden" name="book" value="The Antichrist and the Prophet" />
        <div class="form-row">
          <input
            type="email"
            name="email"
            placeholder="your@email.com"
            required
            aria-label="Email address"
          />
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn--filled">Notify Me at Launch</button>
        </div>
        <p class="form-note muted">
          Your information is never shared. Unsubscribe at any time.
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .book-hero {
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .book-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .byline {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .status-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid var(--gold);
    color: var(--gold);
    padding: 0.3rem 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .logline {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--gold-light);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* PREMISE */
  .premise-body p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
  }

  .premise-body p:first-child {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .premise-body blockquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    color: var(--gold-light);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  /* FIGURES */
  .section--dark {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .figures {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .figure-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .figure p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  /* ABOUT */
  .about-book h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .about-book > .container > p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .themes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .theme h3 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .theme p {
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  /* EMAIL */
  .email-capture h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .email-capture > .container > p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 560px;
  }

  .email-form {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .form-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 520px;
  }

  .form-row input {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .form-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .form-row {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .figures,
    .themes {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
